        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Crosses at $\\left(-\\frac12,0\\right)$ and $(0,25)$; local maximum $\\left(\\frac43,\\frac{1331}{27}\\right)$; touches the $x$-axis at the local minimum $(5,0)$. The left end falls and the right end rises.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-5)^2(2x+1)&=0\\\\x&=5\\text{ or }-\\frac12,\\\\y(0)&=(0-5)^2(2\\cdot0+1)\\\\y(0)&=25.\\end{align*}$$\nThe simple root $x=-\\frac12$ gives a crossing; the double root $x=5$ gives a touch at the local minimum. The leading term is $2x^3$, so $y\\to-\\infty$ as $x\\to-\\infty$ and $y\\to\\infty$ as $x\\to\\infty$. Add the stationary points found in part b.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p22-q15-graph",
